<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Nihomano Sigils ~ the record

The cultural contract speaks at <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nihomano-sigils`>>. This record keeps what the first-discovered set's slot counted and named as owed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/first-census`>>

!! The first census

> The nihomano discovery yielded the first coherent set of SharktoothSigil-registered sigils. The set holds 47 tiddlers, each carrying a pono law spec and passing the alignment check. They fall into eight families.

The sigil tiddler shelf (`packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/sigil-*.tid`) names the set as it stands; a count in prose ages as the shelf grows.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/define-alias`>>

!! The `\define` line

The set's pragma list read: ''`\define` — backward-compat alias; use `\procedure` instead''. The mirror vocabulary states the present rule: `\define` mirrors `wehe` read-only, and `meme normalize` re-mints it as `wehe`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/tag-companion-work`>>

!! The tag's companion work

> The migration from `$:/` to `lar:///` namespaces across all owned tags is the companion sprint to this one.

The tag bullet also read: ''Readable by `grammar-cache.ts` via `wiki.filterTiddlers([tag[lar:///ha.ka.ba/tags/SharktoothSigil]])` — tiddler sigils take precedence over TOML fallback by name.'' No TOML fallback stands in `grammar-cache.ts`; the api meme names the filter and the `lar-name` rule the cache reads.

<<~/ahu>>

